17592186045417] [17592186510410 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510410 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118277" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510410 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510410 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f0/f05b638b28790b3bc87bc8e76b10092fdd13dde6d4c3dc98b93c7e92401f28fc.png)\n\nConsider the diagram shown above. Which of the following could be $-a?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510410 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "78aa3546-9c22-5075-a931-7cce83bce972" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510410 #edb/ref 1074 "The vector $-a$ has the same magnitude as $a$ but goes in the direction opposite to $a$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/c5/c5fb5b587a0e0f72cd73a7439420d153562dffec79f15e9dfa46e5167ac85196.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510432 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510432 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510432 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510432 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/70/70fe7561f7019a01ea671190c26e3d73f8918fcd18172d0c3e3a1a9447d7269e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector addition $a+b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510432 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a1cc494e-dcbc-545c-8007-d17190e50a46" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510432 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we draw the vector that is equal to $b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $a.$ \n\nNow, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant \n\n$$\na+b\n$$\n\nis the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/7c/7c6a56945cc2a8cefb2ad29114ee5979196de6df7415d064dc0b5b841f5e466b.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510437 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510331 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510437 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118284" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510437 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510437 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/98/98619223439f3dbbb12f7849bfdb787ef952245569c16e7edf59b07ef908abd0.png)\n\nThe diagram shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$  Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector subtraction $a-b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510437 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "a6578d74-834c-5f37-879c-4ad4b226d0f1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510437 #edb/ref 1074 "We interpret the subtraction\n$a-b$\nas the addition\n\n$$\na+(-b),\n$$\n\nwhere $-b$ is the vector that has the same magnitude as $b$ but goes in the direction *opposite* of $b.$\n\nFinally, we use the triangle law to add the vectors $a$ and $-b:$ \n\n- We can start $a$ from an arbitrary point on the plane.\n\n- Next, we draw the vector that is equal to $-b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $a.$\n\n- Now, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $-\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/09/0990751c1d413600cba164bd50b732742b73ccc8bc0bcf3a3c039bc3693d8d5f.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510440 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510440 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118546" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510440 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510440 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/92/926161e90964be4d6d4d32491ce4b6fdfa7e964d5d88ebc4eb7dd367dd2a837f.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a},$ $\\text{b},$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $a-b+c.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510440 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa07fa75-e006-5c8d-9bd3-e38658b1ba33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510440 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\na-b=a+(-b).\n$$\n\nThe resultant $a-b$ is the vector that joins the tail of $\\text{a}$ and the head of $-\\text{b}:$\n\n![](images/a4/a487c6406c591962ce27be6c27006c2d8f2ef49d05ee704007d578788db77883.png)\n\nNow, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\n(\\text{a}-\\text{b})+\\text{c}.\n$$\n\nWe draw $\\text{c}$ from the head of $\\text{a}-\\text{b}.$ So, we have the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{c}:$\n\n![](images/12/122df7ad9d20a94049597c1a75adf75f8286b7e67ca9b9a661029e21fea6393c.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510459 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510459 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69482" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510459 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510459 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/6f/6f1af14d60c9b2353d3aa149c4f74ead097289fd2a619013f1506cb783b72ee2.png)\n\nThe vectors $\\text{a},$ $\\text{b},$ and $\\text{c}$ are shown in the diagram above. Which of the following diagrams shows the vector $a-b-c.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510459 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d8517d92-ae69-5efd-a845-0b2600987e0b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510459 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\na-b=a+(-b).\n$$\n\nThe resultant $a-b$ is the vector that joins the tail of $\\text{a}$ and the head of $-\\text{b}:$\n\n![](images/40/40912329e0fa213a0bb8be143ed2d44441634ced3eaf378d76a69aa3167fe14c.png)\n\nNow, we use the triangle law of addition to find \n\n$$\n(\\text{a}-\\text{b})-\\text{c}=(\\text{a}-\\text{b})+(-\\text{c}).\n$$\n\nWe draw $-\\text{c}$ from the head of $\\text{a}-\\text{b}.$ So, we have the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $-\\text{c}:$\n\n![](images/6c/6cbd0e043e9de98da0044792d5be99df0e1a17eff3b9dc8b87093985c5a27f24.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510474 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510474 #edb/ref 1069 "q-69451" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510474 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510474 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/77/7711469c806f738c8dab65dedee5e86bfb34fd65750e16a8938efd18e1e4dcf9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the vectors $a$ and $b.$ Which of the following diagrams illustrates the vector addition $a+b.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510474 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f374050f-4aee-5c4e-89b5-51002237ae2e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510474 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we draw the vector that is equal to $b$ and has its tail placed at the head of $a.$ \n\nNow, according to the triangle law of addition, the resultant \n\n$$\na+b\n$$\n\nis the vector that goes from the tail of $\\text{a}$ to the head of $\\text{b}$, as shown below.\n\n![](images/45/45b6fbac62a351630908b2ffd732b39249ebe410a950afa55db79a40082ad827.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510477 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186510300 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510477 #edb/ref 1069 "q-118283" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510477 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510477 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/39/392fab62a445326d26f7c637735cb03f13d94139ec0141d1802c8617020b1489.png)\n\nConsider the vector $a,$ shown above. Which of the following could be $a+(-a)?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510477 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fa100519-5f40-5eb3-8aa6-b2668b120fa7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186510477 #edb/ref 1074 "According to the triangle law of addition, the resultant is the vector that goes from the tail of $a$ to the head of $-a.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain a new vector for which the tail and head is the same point, the tail of $a.$ \n\nThat vector is called the zero vector, and we write\n\n$$\na+(-a)=0.\n$$\n\nThe corresponding graph is shown below.\n\n![](images/96/96172072cf76df18a675eb506207756e65b7458e2f3c5fa056f54a81335fc6de.png)" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
